WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
- All right everybody,

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:02.910
we have time for one more uplifting story.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.537
This is "#What I'm Liking"

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.000
So, this month, the "Miss America" pageant

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.370
made history when, for
the very first time,

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.840
they crowned an active-duty
military officer as the winner.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.020
22-year-old second
lieutenant, Madison Marsh,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.960
isn't just a pilot, but that's so cool,

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.380
she's also a graduate
student at Harvard, sure.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.010
And check out her interview
just before she won the pageant.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.010
- [Interviewer] So, as Miss
America, it says that you want

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.810
to go on "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.287
So, let's pretend, you're
walking out as Miss America,

00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:40.080
"Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.480
What is your message as Miss America

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.360
to all of those young girls out there?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.800
- They can do anything that they want.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.020
They can be Miss America,
they can be a military member,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.390
they can be a doctor, lawyer, you name it.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.780
And I think me being able
to be there echoes that

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.190
to women all around the world.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.690
And that's exactly what I wanna do

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.880
and capitalize on in my international plan

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.513
with the Air Force.

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:03.473
- I mean, I love the girl!

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.167
I'm also honored to help
her spread her message.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.670
Let's welcome your 2024 "Miss America"

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.743
Second Lieutenant, Madison Marsh!

00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:14.644
(audience applauding)

00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:18.394
♪ There she is, Miss America ♪

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.151
- This is so crazy!

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:28.735
- It is amazing, look at
what you've accomplished,

00:01:28.735 --> 00:01:29.568
that nobody else has.

00:01:29.568 --> 00:01:31.470
- First of all, thank you
so much for your service.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.820
- Oh, thank you, thank you.

00:01:33.897 --> 00:01:35.640
I mean this, you think this

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.650
is more than a win for you though, right?

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.050
- Absolutely, I mean, I kind
of talked about a little bit

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.330
how it goes more than just me winning

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.730
and how I feel like I get
to represent all women.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.563
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:45.563 --> 00:01:47.040
- Women in the military
being able to show,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.102
like, we can break boundaries,

00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:51.596
and that femininity can be a
superpower and you use that

00:01:51.596 --> 00:01:54.330
to be a leader and they
don't have to be separated

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.650
- [Kelly] Separate, because
I think people do that.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.390
You're either this or
that and you can be both.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.274
I love that message.

00:01:58.274 --> 00:01:59.107
- Yeah.

00:01:59.107 --> 00:01:59.940
- Yeah.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.050
So there was a very
important thing for you

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.150
to be honoring your mom through
this whole process, right?

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.200
- [Madison] Mm hm.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.710
So, I lost my mom to
pancreatic cancer in 2018,

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.770
She was only 41 years
old and was misdiagnosed.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.530
And we had no cancer
history in our family,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.360
she didn't have any of the warning signs.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.320
And so, when she passed
away, I saw how much

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.690
she would've given to
be here to have her life

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.610
and her love shared with everyone.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.490
And I know that I have an
incredible opportunity every day.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.066
Each day that I get is an
opportunity that my mom

00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:32.280
and other pancreatic cancer
patients didn't have,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.630
so that's why we started the Whitney,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.463
- It's a privilege.
- Yeah.

00:02:34.463 --> 00:02:36.754
So that's why we started that
Whitney Marsh Foundation.

00:02:36.754 --> 00:02:38.520
So basically we raise money

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.367
for pancreatic cancer care,
advocacy and the patients.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.820
We do a 5K, 10K every year for my mom

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.960
'cause she's a big runner.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.700
I mean, when she was going
through chemotherapy,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.350
that woman was running 10 miles.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.400
- Oh my gosh.
- So, yeah.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.780
- What a superhero mom.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.860
- I know, I know.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.850
- Yeah, That's incredible.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:57.695
Thank you so much for being
just such a powerful influence

00:02:57.695 --> 00:02:59.985
for young women and young men.

00:02:59.985 --> 00:03:02.044
Like, anybody can do
anything they wanna do.

00:03:02.044 --> 00:03:03.870
You can achieve it, it's
just such a cool thing.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.030
And what a barrier to break

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.130
that nobody even really,
maybe, realized was there.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.080
But, like, yeah, you can be both things.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.510
You can be beautiful and
powerful, and you represent that.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.343
So thank you for doing that.

00:03:13.343 --> 00:03:14.656
- Thank you.

00:03:14.656 --> 00:03:15.489
- Yes, there's so many young people.

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:17.580
Thank you Madison, I'm
liking your post right now.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.450
That is not all though.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.033
Our season long partner
Pilot, pen makers of Precise,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.620
the Go-To pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.630
want to honor truly unstoppable people

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.280
just like you and your mama.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.590
So they are gonna be writing
the Whitney Marsh Foundation

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.415
a check for $1,000, just so you know.

00:03:30.415 --> 00:03:31.473
- Oh my.

00:03:31.473 --> 00:03:34.172
- Thank you so much,
you are so incredible.

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:35.503
- Thank you for having me.

00:03:35.503 --> 00:03:36.694
- Come back any time!

00:03:36.694 --> 00:03:37.713
- Oh, thank you so much.

00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:39.101
- Yeah!

00:03:39.101 --> 00:03:40.590
Thank you to all of our guests this hour,

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.815
Chrissy Teigen, David
Chang, Bianca Belair,

00:03:42.815 --> 00:03:45.602
Montez Ford and Rachel Montez Minor.

00:03:45.602 --> 00:03:50.602
Y'all have a great day,
and if it's not, change it.

